tion/id #uuid "964ace1f-4db9-5484-a2c3-7ffb0c8d5586" :question/math-academy-id "q-317612" :question/problem "A linear transformation $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis. Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(u)=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we are told that $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis.\n\nComparing the $x$- and $y$-components of $u$ and $T(u),$ we note the following:\n\n- the $x$-components of $u$ and $T(u)$ are the same, while\n\n- the $y$-component of $T(u)$ is $\\sqrt{3}$ times the $y$-component of $u.$\n\nSo, we conclude that $T$ represents a stretch of scale factor $\\sqrt{3}$ in the $y$-direction. \n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-317612/field-1" "q-317612/field-2" "q-317612/field-3" "q-317612/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3105e8eb-010f-542b-9e40-12fda6ea00e7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317612"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317609/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "8bc3c941-eb66-5555-8d60-181fe24c7468" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317609/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d8e1473c-1de5-54a0-9237-35db5a9f49d6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317609/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-317609/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317609/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "d68253fd-ff6e-5953-ba8e-bf0bdc15728a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317609/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "856855d4-bc04-506c-9ee3-afedc09171f8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317609/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-317609/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317609/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "391aa0a5-532c-55d0-ad07-9472cf2e0701" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317609/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "517a3563-445f-5c1d-8247-ba695b632bea" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317609/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-317609/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317609" :question/id #uuid "269e92e7-dd9e-5a56-9cb9-162b4eeb2056" :question/math-academy-id "q-317609" :question/problem "A linear transformation $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis. Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(u)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we are told that $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis.\n\nComparing the $x$- and $y$-components of $u$ and $T(u),$ we note the following:\n\n- the $y$-components of $u$ and $T(u)$ are the same, while\n\n- the $x$-component of $T(u)$ is $\\frac{1}{2}$ times the $x$-component of $u.$\n\nSo, we conclude that $T$ represents a stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$ in the $x$-direction. \n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-317609/field-1" "q-317609/field-2" "q-317609/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3105e8eb-010f-542b-9e40-12fda6ea00e7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317609"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-165787/selection/5e2359ca36ad841b2ac85f011c260dfc34fd4fe7d03e392d163abb05fd8b0dad" :answer/id #uuid "fa242814-002b-5051-ab32-2b4072df1c19" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A vertical shear with a shear factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165787/selection/8122f0b3c72c6b374196396fce00493ecd363b11b1d65050561f128bd36d1af7" :answer/id #uuid "6891c862-6f77-5b0a-845a-e7db65e7cb7f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A stretch with a scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$ in the $y$-direction" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165787/selection/01cfe339bebfbc122507e0cbb7162f49b9953b45b292773385b05506127ba8cf" :answer/id #uuid "ad32dc1c-d6e5-519e-ad3a-64466060a392" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A stretch with a scale factor $2$ in the $y$-direction" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165787/selection/e877517131b32004e62bd61b7ac2bac9edf569c596c832e8bbd04ea296890905" :answer/id #uuid "1332c767-1678-5804-b680-ed62af259dab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A stretch with a scale factor $2$ in the $x$-direction" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165787/selection/388805e6c9519ba6e6598641fe9cb47b021dc255cd71ef89c2218046e81ddc78" :answer/id #uuid "91c8635f-aef6-5dfe-8684-c185c31accf1" :answer/type :answer