7/selection/5a148e3e90dd8a742b5bdc5ef51bf5aa7679d4ade1e724d5c16a2187268b35ea" "q-81327/selection/3e6da98bd51d835a6b7427dd971b1d5be04f991920d144930a903c512d898699"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81327" :question/id #uuid "32a103ba-7e9c-5ed8-b8b8-915a57355296" :question/math-academy-id "q-81327" :question/problem "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of ${R}^{2}.$ If $T$ is a linear transformation such that $T(i)=i$ and $T(j)=-i+j,$ then what is the geometric interpretation of the transformation $T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's consider the unit square spanned by the vectors $i$ and $j.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/assets/db15a65fd944c24ea2545baea08e6a0789b749295f623d8d4fdc2f07a37d4b73.png)\n\nNow, using the fact that $T(i)=i$ and $T(j)=-i+j,$ we can draw the image of the square under the transformation $T:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/assets/cee26b17d477344e138c3d6d9228f23d67c4c78ce447b1c2c3a887b79125ee7a.png)\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ represents a horizontal shear with a shear factor of $-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-81327/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "be42e4b3-4b15-589c-a7e1-23cc07083aff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81327"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-12044"] :question/problem "What linear transformation is represented by the following matrix\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the images of the standard basis vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of  $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=i \\\\ T(j) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=10i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a *horizontal* shear with a shear factor of $10.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8092"] :question/problem "What linear transformation is represented by the following matrix\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 12 & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the images of the standard basis vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of  $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 12 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]=i+12j \\\\ T(j) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 12 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a *vertical* shear with a shear factor of $12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-8090/selection/a5885e763ee9ca6a86977c5bfcea5de662282722af0cbffd037fe3865cb443da" :answer/id #uuid "3a0009f1-ffe4-542a-a3c3-93a77b1267eb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A horizontal shear with a shear factor of $5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8090/selection/59165ea2627afdaad5f969228074e3b49bee35cafdcf398b4dfcb9ad877aa532" :answer/id #uuid "9a7cb190-95e5-5253-a016-8e60d9688bf3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A stretch of scale factor $5$ in the $y$-direction" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8090/selection/39d0438bef90ef6db8c9d88b6796e30766d99e5fecbb0178d4624b7bd5a66888" :answer/id #uuid "dbe0a344-dfa2-57cf-b566-0b1c21ed0d44" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A vertical shear with a shear factor of $5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8090/selection/5e2359ca36ad841b2ac85f011c260dfc34fd4fe7d03e392d163abb0