$j$ under the action of  $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=2i \\\\ T(j) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a stretch of scale factor $2$ in the $x$-direction." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8089/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c36ce626-1562-51f8-b3fd-d7dc7ce8659c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8089"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-38066"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/assets/611f958a7bd7475e37f743ef86affde7754195fe2c9ad414e628c17a09d47e38.png)\n\nLet $T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ be the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T.$ What is the image of the square $R$ (shown above) above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Looking at the matrix $T$, we can see that $T$ represents a horizontal shear of shear factor $\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore, the image of the square $R$ under $T$ is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/assets/85ff90a404a22310659fadd3a00c58490c9745d443b180d6b509b40a5497376b.png)\n\n**Alternative method:**\n\nWe can check that the vertices of $R$ are mapped to the vertices of the parallelogram shown above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-165980/selection/f789b118ed4a4647aecf831ceea3a6ca85ad0fe0d6d8781e1399b10944809824" :answer/id #uuid "a54a940b-885e-5cb5-9997-21b1f954a859" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/assets/dae63d7007d115438139be51862d878deadd1ed300b3b870935c2cbe44edaef3.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165980/selection/59bd4b0e0cb92cd655ad7b10b569e4693a514aaa4161dcb6159160cf7dbf6afd" :answer/id #uuid "28813f25-d10a-5c2b-901f-49d755aceed2" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/assets/bfdc9898972e72a5d15c8313eff3403e2ea712e2bffe52b3fd1d9fb6156b7bec.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165980/selection/93ced61f1709659c9079ede4ceec53634e52096292e9685aa579f3aa705aca47" :answer/id #uuid "2519178e-a642-58f2-abe0-1d9d7088099f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/assets/364633d020e330780fab5ea588cca231ecd0e3d3c8e3e5516e4d6d0d990299c0.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165980/selection/4c6063b9952b8e00f3452f14e6df43f64ba2b1efb3fde3c2c61671bb5ec2f9fa" :answer/id #uuid "6bfe53a0-d63f-5285-8d89-c2b5b561fa8e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/